      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7041641139073515,
        "y0": 0.3111397042568035,
        "x1": 0.8121287182135367,
        "y1": 0.32297331643218674
      },
      "text": "and concave in",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8176610661089353,
        "y0": 0.3111397042568035,
        "x1": 0.8272341186063272,
        "y1": 0.32297331643218674
      },
      "text": "u",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8272415009487196,
        "y0": 0.3111397042568035,
        "x1": 0.8318774069061032,
        "y1": 0.32297331643218674
      },
      "text": ",",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930463290675777,
        "y0": 0.3253933478444455,
        "x1": 0.2362497725090179,
        "y1": 0.3372269600198289
      },
      "text": "and",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.24215157075477123,
        "y0": 0.3253933478444455,
        "x1": 0.2724271721013525,
        "y1": 0.3372269600198289
      },
      "text": "U ⊂",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.27834319673609126,
        "y0": 0.3253933478444455,
        "x1": 0.831337547485523,
        "y1": 0.3372269600198289
      },
      "text": "is a convex set, then using duality theory one can derive a tractable robust",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930463290675777,
        "y0": 0.33964699143208765,
        "x1": 0.49060504733308585,
        "y1": 0.351480603607471
      },
      "text": "counterpart reformulation of Problem (",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.490888293456129,
        "y0": 0.33964699143208765,
        "x1": 0.5016328826781874,
        "y1": 0.351480603607471
      },
      "text": "P",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5016328826781874,
        "y0": 0.344972859050397,
        "x1": 0.5206818380977375,
        "y1": 0.35325636423794227
      },
      "text": "rob",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5215362416971288,
        "y0": 0.33964699143208765,
        "x1": 0.8315725776848156,
        "y1": 0.351480603607471
      },
      "text": "). Because of this, the field of convex robust",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.3539006350197297,
        "x1": 0.8312516764889444,
        "y1": 0.36573424719511305
      },
      "text": "optimisation is well-established, whereas the field of non-convex robust optimisation",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.3681542786073718,
        "x1": 0.38322618575610046,
        "y1": 0.3799878907827552
      },
      "text": "is still at its infancy [1].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2344089290405706,
        "y0": 0.38240792219501385,
        "x1": 0.8312685430906605,
        "y1": 0.3942415343703972
      },
      "text": "State-of-the-art robust optimisation algorithms for non-convex problems typically",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.396661565782656,
        "x1": 0.8313185277006092,
        "y1": 0.40849517795803936
      },
      "text": "rely on global solvers to obtain robust optimal solutions. The prevailing approach",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.41091520937029813,
        "x1": 0.8311847227447463,
        "y1": 0.4227488215456814
      },
      "text": "involves deriving the dual reformulation and utilising a global solver, either directly",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.42516885295794016,
        "x1": 0.8312683892918605,
        "y1": 0.4370024651333235
      },
      "text": "or adaptively. However, the dual reformulation can increase the problem complexity,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.4394224965455823,
        "x1": 0.8313353430360586,
        "y1": 0.45125610872096567
      },
      "text": "and in the case of challenging non-convex problems may only yield a robust feasible",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.4536761401332243,
        "x1": 0.8312851020947768,
        "y1": 0.4655097523086077
      },
      "text": "solution. An alternative approach is based on an iterative robust cutting plane algo-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.46792978372086647,
        "x1": 0.8313019174302262,
        "y1": 0.47976339589624983
      },
      "text": "rithm. In this case, significant computational time can be spent searching for a global",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.4821834273085085,
        "x1": 0.55237797642593,
        "y1": 0.49401703948389186
      },
      "text": "solution that may be deemed robust infeasible.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2344089290405706,
        "y0": 0.49643707089615063,
        "x1": 0.8315115451944115,
        "y1": 0.508270683071534
      },
      "text": "Contributions of this work: Our research hypothesis is that integrated explo-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.5106907144837927,
        "x1": 0.8312517790214776,
        "y1": 0.5225243266591761
      },
      "text": "ration of global and robust optimality can yield computational benefits. To this end, in",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.5249443580714348,
        "x1": 0.8312851020947768,
        "y1": 0.5367779702468182
      },
      "text": "this article we introduce a novel algorithm that conducts a concurrent global optimal-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.5391980016590769,
        "x1": 0.8313186302331425,
        "y1": 0.5510316138344602
      },
      "text": "ity and robustness search for continuous non-convex problems. The proposed approach",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.553451645246719,
        "x1": 0.8312683892918605,
        "y1": 0.5652852574221023
      },
      "text": "integrates spatial branch-and-bound with robust cutting plane notions. The key idea",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.567705288834361,
        "x1": 0.8312851020947768,
        "y1": 0.5795389010097445
      },
      "text": "is that, while exploring the branch-and-bound tree, we assess the robustness of nodes",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.5819589324220031,
        "x1": 0.8312517790214776,
        "y1": 0.5937925445973865
      },
      "text": "entailing the best-found solutions. We illustrate the performance and benefits of our",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.5962125760096453,
        "x1": 0.8313353430360586,
        "y1": 0.6080461881850286
      },
      "text": "proposed approach through benchmark Quadratically Constrained Quadratic Pro-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6104662195972874,
        "x1": 0.8313520558389749,
        "y1": 0.6222998317726707
      },
      "text": "grams (QCQPs) of pooling problems. At each node, the non-convex problem is solved",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6247198631849294,
        "x1": 0.831385378912274,
        "y1": 0.6365534753603128
      },
      "text": "via a local solver. If the computed solution is as good as the best-found so far, an",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6389735067725715,
        "x1": 0.8312181483505787,
        "y1": 0.650807118947955
      },
      "text": "infeasibility test is performed to evaluate the robustness of the obtained solution. If",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6532271503602136,
        "x1": 0.8313018148976931,
        "y1": 0.665060762535597
      },
      "text": "not, then the corresponding cutting planes are added both to the non-convex and con-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6674807939478558,
        "x1": 0.8313354455685918,
        "y1": 0.679314406123239
      },
      "text": "vex problems. The algorithm proceeds to the next step once no more violations are",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6817344375354978,
        "x1": 0.8312516764889444,
        "y1": 0.6935680497108812
      },
      "text": "detected. The convex problem is solved next, and the solution of this problem is used",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.6959880811231399,
        "x1": 0.83128520462731,
        "y1": 0.7078216932985233
      },
      "text": "to decide the most promising variable for branching into two child nodes. With the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.710241724710782,
        "x1": 0.8312851020947768,
        "y1": 0.7220753368861654
      },
      "text": "use of appropriate fathoming criteria, the tree nodes are exhausted, and the robust",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20930460727362446,
        "y0": 0.7244953682984241,
        "x1": 0.41847241051478906,
        "y1": 0.7363289804738075
      },
      "text": "optimal solution is obtained.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5164142289997098,
        "y0": 0.7634185021904798,
        "x1": 0.5247822679003364,
        "y1": 0.7752521143658632
      },
      "text": "2",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
